# DMR Codeplug & Linux Hardware Rules

- Always validate DMR channel definitions in `qdmrcodeplug.yaml`:
  - Every digital channel MUST define `radioId`, `rxFrequency`, `txFrequency`, `colorCode`, `timeSlot`, and `groupList`.
  - Never allow empty `radioId: ""` (causes yaml-cpp exception in qdMR).
- USB cable access requires user in `dialout` group and udev rules under `/etc/udev/rules.d/`.
- For Python codeplug automation, strictly use `ruamel.yaml` with `round_trip_dump` to prevent dropping comments and reordering keys.
